A call whose closing `)` was dropped. unclosed_delimiter reports the
opener (where the fix belongs). The catalog says such an opener swallows
the rest of the file into that statement, so unexpected_token must defer
for everything after it; records whether block pairing downstream is
disturbed (diag.unclosed_delimiter, diag.unexpected_token deferral).
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE NoteLength;
	:PARAMETERS sNote;
	:DECLARE nLen;
	nLen := Len(AllTrim(sNote);
	:IF nLen > 200;
		nLen := 200;
	:ENDIF;
	:RETURN nLen;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE NoteLength;
	:PARAMETERS sNote;
	:DECLARE nLen;
	nLen := Len(AllTrim(sNote);
	            :IF nLen > 200;
	            nLen := 200;
	            :ENDIF;
	            :RETURN nLen;
	            :ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
4:13-4:14 error unclosed_delimiter: Unclosed '('
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
4:13-4:14 error unclosed_delimiter: Unclosed '('
